WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.259
The rules, in order.

2
00:00:01.539 --> 00:00:05.336
Classify every failure: transient, permanent, or refusal.

3
00:00:05.616 --> 00:00:13.232
Retry only transient ones, at one layer, with capped exponential backoff and full jitter, treating retry-after as a minimum.

4
00:00:13.512 --> 00:00:17.608
Give each request one deadline, and size each attempt to what remains.

5
00:00:17.888 --> 00:00:21.344
Make side effects idempotent before you let anything retry.

6
00:00:21.624 --> 00:00:25.592
Put a breaker in front of each dependency so a dead one fails fast.

7
00:00:25.872 --> 00:00:33.083
Fall back to another model on outages and refusals, record that you did, and know from an eval what it costs you in quality.

8
00:00:33.363 --> 00:00:35.773
Keep a degraded mode and exercise it.

9
00:00:36.053 --> 00:00:40.960
And test all of this with fakes, because the real failures arrive on their own schedule.
